#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/annotations/index.rst:90
msgid ""
"@T.prim_func\n"
"def kernel(src: T.Tensor((N,), T.float32), dst: T.Tensor((N,), T.float32)):\n"
"    T.annotate_host_mapped_buffers(dst)\n"
"    with T.Kernel(T.ceildiv(N, 128), threads=128) as block:\n"
"        ..."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/annotations/index.rst:96
msgid ""
"Currently supported by the CUDA Cython and TVM-FFI launchers. Annotated "
"buffers must be supplied explicitly as CPU tensors with registered/mapped "
"storage (for example, PyTorch tensors allocated with ``pin_memory=True``). "
"Other tensor checks remain enabled. This annotation does not allocate, "
"register, copy, or synchronize memory. The caller must keep the storage and "
"mapping alive until GPU work completes, and throughout graph replay, and "
"synchronize before accessing or reusing that storage on the CPU."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/annotations/index.rst:104
msgid ""
"The contract applies to the whole function, even when this declaration is "
"inside a kernel block. Repeated declarations are merged."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/annotations/index.rst:112
msgid ""
"This annotation tells codegen to omit the `__restrict__` qualifier for the "
"specified kernel buffer parameters. Use this when two (or more) buffers may "
"alias, for example overlapping slices from the same base tensor."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/annotations/index.rst:128
msgid ""
"Declare the depth of the pipelines the automatic scheduler hosts at the "
"ENCLOSING scope for the given buffers, asserting each recurrence resets per "
"version — otherwise the depth derives from the loop's ``num_stages``, and "
"accumulators pin single-buffered."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/annotations/index.rst:133
msgid "``depth_map`` maps each buffer to its pipeline depth at this scope."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/annotations/index.rst:140
msgid ""
"``schedule`` is a "
"typed :class:`~tilelang.language.warp_specialize.WSSchedule` object "
"describing how to transform the straight-line kernel into a warp-specialized "
"one: warp roles, pipelines (full/empty barrier pairs protecting multi-"
"versioned buffers), and per-role instruction sequences per loop scope. It is "
"materialized by the ``MaterializeWSSchedule`` pass; see ``examples/aws/"
"gemm.py`` for a complete example."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/annotations/index.rst:150
msgid ""
"Manually annotate the enclosed statement(s) with a stable warp-"
"specialization op or scope id."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/annotations/index.rst:153
msgid ""
"Wraps the body in an ``AttrStmt`` with key :data:`WSID`. This is the "
"annotation of last resort, for statement forms that cannot carry "
"``annotations=`` themselves. The enclosed statements — a scalar Bind, or "
"several statements such as an inlined scheduler method — become ONE opaque "
"op:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/annotations/index.rst:164
msgid ""
"With a scope id the wrapper encloses a ``while`` loop and opens that scope "
"(serial scope loops carry the id in their own annotations):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/annotations/index.rst:171
msgid "Tile ops and loops pass ``annotations={T.WSID: ...}`` directly instead."
msgstr ""
